"Important engine of global recovery"-China News Network
“In response to the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic, China’s economy has shown great resilience.
Recent market expectations indicate that the international community is generally positive about China’s future development.
Julio Ríos, a renowned Spanish expert on China and honorary advisor to the China Policy Observatory Network, said in an interview with the newspaper that China's current epidemic prevention and control has entered a new phase, and the dynamics of economic and social development will be further unleashed.
Mr. Ríos said that China had responded to shocks from various unexpected factors with extraordinary economic governance experience and measures, which fully reflected its economic resilience and level of management.
China is firmly committed to expanding its opening up to the outside world while the internal driving force of economic development is continuously strengthened, and state-owned enterprises and private enterprises develop in tandem.
Every year at the National People’s Congress and the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, representatives and committee members discuss national development plans and hot issues in people's livelihoods together, widely pooling consensus, gathering hearts, and aggregating wisdom to add strength to China's progress.
“Since reform and opening up, China has achieved long-term high-speed development and is now entering a high-quality development phase.
The international community looks to China for wisdom and solutions, hoping that China’s development will bring new opportunities to the world.
Riose said that China is now making every effort to promote science and technology innovation and inject new momentum into economic and social development, "financial investment, talent development, and policy incentives, which keep China dynamic in the new five-year plan."
In Rio’s view, economic institutional reform is a daunting task for any country.
Under the leadership of the Chinese Communist Party, China has taken active measures to stabilize its economy, using both the strengths of the market economy and the superiority of the socialist system.
Around the strategic base of expanding domestic demand, China will strengthen financial support for the real economy, support the development of private enterprises, small and medium-sized enterprises and manufacturing industry, insist on innovative development, promote employment, improve the income and living standards of the Chinese people, and meet the diverse and multi-layered consumption needs of the people. China will fully, accurately and comprehensively implement the new development concept, focus on promoting high-quality development, build a new development pattern, and bring more growth opportunities to the world.
This year marks the tenth anniversary of the Belt and Road Initiative.
“A stable economic recovery from the pandemic is a common goal of the international community.
China’s economic potential is constantly being unleashed, bringing more benefits to the world and becoming an important engine for global recovery.
"Rios said he expects the joint construction of "Belt and Road" cooperation to continue to play its important role in improving the infrastructure level of countries and strengthening connectivity in all areas, and continue to unleash greater momentum.
(This newspaper reports from Madrid)
(People's Daily, reporter Yang Ying)
The fitness industry should shake off its trust crisis - China News Service
Another large gym “bankruptcy”?
Recently, the issue of protecting the rights of members of a well-known fitness institution, Zhongxin Fitness, has attracted social attention.
After the Spring Festival, many members found that their stores were not operating normally. Subsequently, rumors about the agency going bankrupt and running away caused members to panic, leading to the involvement of public security and social welfare departments.
Finally, the relevant person in charge of the agency came forward to respond, promising to strive to safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of employees and members, and the storm was finally calmed down.
Some fitness institutions have temporarily closed some of their branches due to operational problems. Consumers could have waited for the problems to be solved calmly. Why did many members' first reaction be "something is wrong"?
Behind the fitness club membership dispute is an underlying issue of industry trust crisis.
In China, traditional gyms generally adopt a prepaid payment model, and “making money from users who don’t come” is the underlying logic of its development.
By obtaining cash flow through pre-sale of membership cards and opening new stores, it seems that the cycle can be repeated, but in fact, it is eating the rice of the other, and it is impossible to form a stable profit model.
Negative publicity about fitness centers and other industries is frequently circulating, severely undermining consumer confidence.
From a market perspective, gyms can certainly be considered a good business opportunity.
The fitness market is cyclical but remains under capital attention.
Multiple data show that interest in cultural and entertainment consumption is on the rise, with the market showing signs of recovery.
Specific to the fitness market, with steady improvement in residents' living standards and widespread acceptance of healthy-living concepts, there is great potential for growth in the industry.
As the situation improves, the industry will have to focus on quality development.
However, some institutions are overly optimistic about the fitness market after the recovery of consumption, and just after coming out of the crisis, they are blowing the horn of expanding the market and investing all the funds in the construction of new stores.
It is undeniable that in recent years, many institutions have withdrawn due to the epidemic, and the industry has undergone a reshuffle. At this time, powerful enterprises choose to increase the acquisition intensity and reorganize, which is a new opportunity.
However, in order to develop into a virtuous cycle and move towards a prosperous future, the fitness industry must change its traditional model and business strategy.
Only by standing firm and rebuilding consumers' confidence and sense of security can we truly win the market and win the future.
Rather than building new stores to capture market share, the fitness industry needs to focus on improving service quality and achieving sustainable growth to stabilize users.
First, we need to rely on services to retain users.
Gyms belong to the service industry, and their essence is to adhere to “user orientation”. They should focus on the needs of users and improve the quality of services.
Secondly, digital transformation is necessary to improve user experience.
For example, the Internet gym model, which is now popular, allows users to pay per session and choose their own venue.
At the same time, body data and movement data can be used effectively, and can also meet social needs, achieving a complete closed loop of services from online to offline.
Without private coaching and huge annual fees, users’ concerns about “running away” from gyms have been reduced, and their trust in gyms has been improved.
In addition, we should actively explore multiple business models.
Today, sports consumption is moving from single-service to scenario-based consumption, with fitness clubs poised to become new entry points for consumption. Products and services related to physical exercise such as supplements and fitness equipment may become new revenue sources, offering consumers more choices.
Jiang Tianjiao
Buy cheap and return the difference!
Nanjing Real Estate Market Revisits "Price Difference Compensation" - China Daily
According to a report by Yangzhou Evening News/Qiwei News, a journalist found out during an interview that the “protection agreement” which had not been seen for more than ten years had returned to the Nanjing real estate market. A property developer in the Nanjing New Area claimed to “pay for the difference” and offered a discount on other properties before the handover of the property, and the developer was willing to switch the property with the buyer and return the difference.
The "Guaranteed Value Agreement" conditions aren't few.
This residential project located in Jiangbei New District is called Baoji Yanzhong Cuiyun Tai and Mr. Sun, who came to view it last weekend, told reporters that he had noticed an announcement while touring the site.
The pictures he sent to reporters showed that the developer of the property promised that if the buyer purchased the property between February 1 and February 28, the developer would switch the property and return the difference if there was a better discount on other properties of the same type (limited to other unsold properties of the same floor plan, same building, same unit, and same property type).
Mr. Sun said that the real estate consultant said that this was actually a "price protection agreement", which was intended to reassure buyers that they did not have to worry about the developer reducing the price for a sale promotion, "Now I'm afraid that it will be reduced in price after I buy it. I don't have time to go to the sales office to make trouble. If I don't make trouble, I will feel relieved."
Many home buyers also believe that the “protection agreement” is a kind of “assurance” for home buyers, but the conditions are not low.
Ms. Zheng, who is planning to buy a starter home in Nanchang, said that properties with price protection were first limited to the same floor plan and had to be located on the same building block as well as within the same unit. Buyers could not compare prices easily, so the “barrier” was still quite high.
Some home buyers also think that because of information asymmetry, the seller may give additional discounts, and it is not easy for buyers to “stand up for their rights”.
Is it possible to retain home buyers remains to be seen.
A reporter inquired about the property on Ningbo's online real estate website and found that the two buildings of the project, with a total of 252 units, were sold in November last year. The unit areas were 105 square meters, 114 square meters, and 129 square meters, and the selling price of fully furnished units was 39,843 yuan/square meter.
However, more than two months have passed, and the online real estate shows that the total number of unsold units in the project is currently 157 units, accounting for 62.3%, of which 128 units are in block 8, and the total number of unsold units is 113; 44 units are unsold in block 7, which has 124 units; the total number of transactions in the project is only 33 units, accounting for only 13%.
Market participants note that “price protection agreements” were also in place in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of that year, the building on Huangshan Road, Hebei, Yongkang West Yard to attract the attention of buyers, introduced the Guaranteed Price Plan, the specific content of which is "the company solemnly promises that if the project's concessions are expanded within a year, the resulting difference, the company will refund the difference to the old owner."
In April 2011, Nanjing also had nine projects that promised “price compensation” for some of their units.
“The property market is recovering, and we need a ‘stimulant’ at this time. ”
Mr. Shen, a senior trader in the Nanjing real estate industry, said that “price guarantee agreements” are also one of the marketing methods of real estate companies.
He argues that developers need confidence more than buyers do, and that the introduction of “price guarantee agreements” is actually encouraging them.
Whether it is possible to retain buyers depends on multiple factors such as policy regulation and loan thresholds; at present, this remains to be seen.
China's rescue team continues to carry out rescue operations in Turkey and has rescued four trapped individuals so far - Xinhua News Agency
China Rescue Team dispatched three operation teams and 45 rescuers to search and rescue in Turkey on February 10, and rescued one person who was trapped.
At the same time, two search and assessment teams were sent to assess and investigate the 15 buildings on Vodabashi Street.
To date, four trapped persons have been rescued, five victims have been searched and life signs and risk assessments have been conducted in 25 buildings that have collapsed severely.
The rescue teams will adjust their rescue forces scientifically according to the actual situation in the disaster area and the rescue site, and will carry out continuous and in-depth rescue work.
The rescue team obtained information about the requests for assistance through embassies, local governments, United Nations relief organizations and other sources, and verified each case by means of online inquiries and on-site searches.
The Hong Kong rescue team was briefed on the current rescue situation and the collapse of buildings, and joint search operations were carried out.
Currently, it is responsible for regional coordination (SSC5) jointly with Italian rescue team, and 3 members are dispatched to participate in the work of the Rescue Coordination Center of Region No. 5. Communication is carried out with Italian, British, Serbian, Slovakian, Omani and other rescue teams to learn about the rescue work of the United Nations rescue organization and rescue teams of various countries.
The rescue team continuously strengthens safety management and personnel support, adhering to the principle of unified command and prioritizing safety, enhancing on-site safety control, strengthening work discipline requirements, and clearly defining safety precautions.
Establish a system of continuous on-call duty and guard duty, and strengthen the security management of the camp.
The medical staff of the rescue team provides medical examination services for the team members every day, and strengthens the medical protection of key personnel. At present, all the members of the rescue team are in good health, and carry out disinfection in the camp.
After establishing their own camps, the logistics security team members built 26 field battle tents of four main categories, including command communications, equipment storage, medical cleaning, living accommodation and dog shelters, and secured more than 30 sets of field rescue equipment.
Kim Jong-un and his daughter interacted intimately, while his wife was left out
(Combined report on 11th) North Korea held a military parade on the 8th evening to celebrate the 75th anniversary of its founding. The daughter of the leader Kim Jong-un, Kim Ju-ae, not only attended the ceremony, but also stood on the podium with her father.
On the 9th, the Korean official media released a video in which Kim Jong-un hugged his father, and they exchanged affectionate glances and whispered to each other several times. She gently held her father's cheek with her hands and even touched her father's chest. The interaction between father and daughter was broadcasted to the whole country.
First lady Li Keqiang, however, was forced to step aside.
According to the reports of “Korea News” and other Korean media, on the 7th, Kim Jong-un and his wife Ri Sol-ju brought their daughter Kim Ju-ae to attend the official photo of the banquet. Not only did Kim Ju-ae sit in the C position in the middle of her parents, which is rare, but she also stood on the podium with Kim Jong-un during the military parade on the 75th anniversary of the founding of the army the next evening.
The Korean Central Television, a Korean official media, later released a film of the parade, revealing more scenes of deep father-daughter love.
Kim Jong-nam frequently looked at his daughter from the podium and never lost their smiles; they also whispered to each other in hushed tones. Kim Chol-ae once cupped her father’s cheeks with both hands, while Kim Jong-nam reciprocated with a radiant smile.
Other official media footage shows Kim Jong-un and Kim Jong-il sitting on a sofa in the room, with Kim’s hands touching her father’s face; and walking with her father, with her hands touching Kim’s chest.
And First Lady Li Keqiang has been forced to walk behind or sit aside, always a few steps away from her husband and daughter.
According to the Korean media, Kim Jong-un has been increasingly exposed in public since the first time he appeared in public after the test-firing of the Mars-17 missile on November 18, 2017. This is the fifth time he has appeared in an official setting in the past three months.
The official media used the highest titles of dearest son and honourable son when referring to Kim Jong-il, and broadcast a scene in which Kim Jong-il repeatedly shouted his death oath to the Whitehead bloodline while standing in the stands overlooking the parade.
These signs have raised doubts about whether Kim Jong-il has been internalized as the successor to the Kim regime, with the Washington Post analysing it as “a signal that Kim is pushing his high-school-aged daughter into succession.” However, some have suggested that such a judgment is premature, and that possibilities remain open with a son in Kim’s lap.
Xinhua News Commentator: Promoting the modernization of China is a systematic project – four thoughts on deeply understanding the important speech of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar on studying and implementing the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress – chinanews.com
Beijing, Feb. 11 (Xinhua) -- The promotion of Chinese-style modernization is a systemic project -- Four points to understand the importance of the opening speech of Secretary-General Xi Jinping at the seminar on learning and implementing the spirit of the Party's 20th Congress
Xinhua News Agency commentator
“Promoting Chinese-style modernization is a systemic project that requires comprehensive consideration, systematic planning and overall advancement, and the correct handling of a series of important relationships, such as top-level design and practical exploration, strategy and tactics, integrity and innovation, efficiency and equity, dynamism and order, self-reliance and openness to the outside world.
“In the opening ceremony of the Seminar on Learning and Implementing the Thought of Xi Jinping on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics in the New Era and the Spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress for the newly elected members of the CPC Central Committee, alternate members and provincial and ministerial leaders, Xi Jinping, the General Secretary, scientifically grasped the laws of modernization construction, and profoundly and systematically explained a series of major relationships that need to be handled in practice, providing a scientific methodology for us to vigorously promote the Chinese-style modernization.
The promotion of China’s modernization involves various fields such as economy, politics, culture, society, and ecological civilization, touching on aspects like governance, national defense, internal security, and foreign policy. It requires both systematic planning and bold innovation to achieve comprehensive advancement.
The design at the top level requires a deep insight into the world &apos; s development trends, a precise understanding of the common aspirations of the people, and a deep exploration of the laws of economic and social development. The planned system and policy must be modern, systematic, creative, closely integrated, consistent from top to bottom, and harmonized in content.
Pushing forward the modernization of China is a venture of exploration, and there are many unknown areas that need to be dared to explore in practice, and drive the development of the industry through reform and innovation, and never be over-cautious.
Strategic issues are fundamental issues for a political party and a country.
To advance China’s modernization model, we must enhance strategic foresight to foresee and lead the future with scientific strategic vision; strengthen global strategy to address major issues that affect the rise and fall of the country’s cause and its overall development; and ensure stability in our strategies so they can be implemented consistently over time and achieved successfully.
To scientifically grasp the dialectical unity of strategy and tactics, integrate their principles with their flexibility, be flexible and adaptable, respond to changes in circumstances, and make decisions on the spot, seize opportunities, and gain strategic initiative in accordance with local conditions, situational considerations, and favorable trends.
The Chinese nation is a nation that is both upright and innovative.
In order to deal with the relationship between innovation and integrity, we must safeguard the essence, origin, roots and soul of Chinese-style modernization, firmly adhere to the Chinese characteristics, essential requirements and major principles of Chinese-style modernization and ensure the correct direction of Chinese-style modernization. At the same time, we must place innovation at the forefront of the overall national development, respond to the development requirements of the time, focus on solving major theoretical and practical problems, actively recognize changes and respond to changes, vigorously promote reform and innovation, continually shape new development dynamics and advantages, and fully stimulate the creative dynamism of the whole society.
Efficiency is an important basis for fairness, and fairness is a powerful guarantee for efficiency.
We are pursuing the Chinese-style modernization, which aims to create greater efficiency than capitalism, while at the same time more effectively preserving social equity, and better achieving the balance, promotion and unification of efficiency and equity.
By balancing efficiency and fairness, we will continuously achieve development for the people, development relying on the people, and development results shared by the people, so that the fruits of modernization will benefit more and more people in a more fair and equitable way.
To advance China-style modernization, we need to deal with the relationship between dynamism and order, so that society is both dynamic and stable.
To effectively balance development and security, we must uphold the overall national security perspective, strengthen the national security system, enhance capabilities for maintaining national security, and resolutely safeguard state sovereignty, regime safety, ideological security, and the security of key areas.
China has taken greater account of security aspects in its development, enhanced national security through development and used development achievements to strengthen the basis of national security. It has also been able to create a security environment conducive to economic and social development, continuously stimulating development dynamism and achieving a positive interaction between high-quality development and a high level of security.
To advance China-style modernization, we must not only stick to our own path, but also broaden our worldview, remain open to the world and constantly expand the breadth and depth of China-style modernization.
We must maintain our independence and self-reliance, and we must insist on placing national and ethnic development on the basis of our own strength. We must insist on firmly holding the fate of our country &apos; s development and progress in our own hands.
We must continuously expand the high level of openness to the outside world, participate in depth in the global division of labour and industrial cooperation, make good use of domestic and international resources, expand the space for China-style modernization, share development opportunities in a win-win environment and jointly create a better future.
Follow the path to achieve far-reaching goals.
Under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee, with Comrade Xi Jinping as its core, and under the scientific guidance of Xi Jinping &apos; s socialist ideas with Chinese characteristics for the new era, let us grasp the rules, act with perseverance, fully use our energy, initiative and creativity, correctly deal with a series of important relations, strive to achieve the new goal of comprehensive construction of a socialist modernized country, and continuously open up new territory for modernization in the Chinese style.
The United States, Japan, and the Philippines have reached a consensus on defense against the CCP
ASIA – On February 9, Philippine President Bongbong Marcos visited Japan to meet Prime Minister Fumio Kishida.
Both sides reached consensus on opposing the CCP's infringement on the South China Sea and the East China Sea. The leaders of the Philippines and Japan issued a joint statement after the meeting, saying that they would sign a trilateral defense agreement with the United States and conduct substantive defense exchanges to oppose the CCP's hegemonic policy.
According to Japanese media reports, Kishida hopes that this meeting will help Japan and the Philippines establish policies for dealing with the crisis in the Taiwan Strait.
Marcos Jr. visited China in early January, and secured a $20 billion deal.
But after that, the relations between China and the Philippines not only did not improve, but rather deteriorated.
Last month, the Philippines signed an agreement with the US to open up more bases for American forces and secure the South China Sea’s security.
One of the new bases is located 300 kilometres from Taiwan, which is also one of the closest locations to China.
If a crisis occurs in Taiwan, the US military may launch an operation from the base in the Philippines.
The Japanese media now believes that Japan, Korea, Taiwan, and even the Philippines are forming an axis with the US, building a “confrontational arc against the CCP” in the Western Pacific to promote regional cooperation.
China Encourages High Fertility Rates and Recruits Donors to Universities for Quality Testing
On 9 September, the Yunnan Province Human Sperm Bank in China issued a notice to solicit sperm donors with a university or higher education or students who successfully donate 8 to 12 times to receive a subsidy of RMB 4,500.
According to Taiwanese media reports today, the message went viral on Weibo on the same day, and triggered the follow-up initiatives of many provinces and cities, including Zhejiang, Shaanxi, Hubei, Shandong and Beijing.
According to a report by the Free Times, China encourages university students to donate sperm.
The universities in different regions donate sperm. The threshold for donating sperm in Beijing is the highest. In addition to academic qualifications, the donor must be taller than 170 cm, have a good appearance, no obvious hair loss, and the degree of myopia cannot be higher than 600 degrees.
According to the report, the Yunnan Human Sperm Bank stated that sperm donors can receive a complete set of men's health tests worth 1,000 yuan, "especially sperm and chromosome tests, which most people have never done, and are important for understanding their fertility status."
The conditions for sperm donors include a height of 165 cm or above, a college education or above, no color blindness, and no genetic diseases or infectious diseases.
The report cited China Tianmu News as saying that the human sperm bank in Shaanxi province had printed a poster with the slogan “Paid sperm donation, unlimited glory,” calling on young people to respond to sperm donation and encouraging netizens to pass on the message, “letting love pass on.”
In Shaanxi Province, the price is higher than that in Yunnan. Qualified people can receive RMB 300 in cash each time, and those who complete a certain number of donations can receive RMB 5,000 subsidies.
The highest known price is in Beijing, where the maximum subsidized price is RMB 5,150.
“Fund E account” has arrived: the CSRC authorized its development; all funds under the name of investors can be collected and queried - Economic Observation Network － a professional financial news website
Economic Observer reporter Chen Shan How difficult is it to aggregate account information due to the proliferation of fund purchase channels?
Always forgetting the “petty cash”?
The problems of the Kievan people will soon be resolved.
On February 10, the SEC announced that the "Fund E Account" APP was listed in various mobile application stores and conducted a public trial.
It is reported that "Fund E Account" provides one-stop query services for individual investors to obtain information on public offering fund accounts and shares, aiming to address industry pain points such as forgetting account numbers and querying them in a cumbersome manner.
According to Wind data, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 public fund managers in China, managing fund assets of about 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 public fund share registration institutions, and 411 public fund sales institutions.
The accounting systems of the various share registers are independent of each other and there is no industry-wide access to them.
Industry observers say that at the end of 2021, there were over 72 million fund investors in China, meaning that half of the country’s population had invested in funds.
Previously, investors had to search for purchases through different sales agencies, but with the “fund E account” they can search for purchases through all sales channels, and have a clear view of the fund holdings.
What is the Fund E-Account App?
According to the relevant documents, the “Fund E Account” APP is a mobile application developed and constructed by China Securities for the public fund industry, approved by the China Securities Regulatory Commission. It can provide investors with one-stop inquiry of off-exchange shareholding of all public fund products in the market.
Investors can easily and quickly manage their holdings of off-the-shelf shares of publicly traded fund products under the management of various fund managers purchased through various sales channels throughout the market through "fund e-account", which improves the efficiency of querying.
Specifically, the information that investors can access through the Fund E Account includes information on fund accounts opened with publicly traded fund managers across the market, information on trading accounts opened with publicly traded fund sales agencies, and information on off-site shareholdings in products such as publicly-received portfolio investment funds and collective asset management plans that are managed by securities companies and have a maximum of 200 investors.
According to Liu Yicheng, the person in charge of the business of Shanghai Securities Fund Evaluation Research Center, investors can know the holdings of all their off-exchange public funds through the "Fund E Account" App, which helps them find "forgotten assets" and, more importantly, helps customers collect comprehensive information on their fund investment, which allows customers to grasp their investment situation more timely, accurate and complete, and thus better optimize their fund portfolio and plan their financial arrangements.
How to register for use?
Journalists have noted that the “Fund E Account” app has been made available on Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and Vivo app stores but is still in public beta testing phase; users need to fill an invitation code during registration, and investors can contact their respective fund managers for assistance.
A customer service representative at a large public-equity fund in Shanghai provided a six-digit invitation code to the Economic Observer, and told the reporter, “During the app’s trial run, China Settlement will provide a certain number of invitation codes to each fund manager, and investors will call us to get them.
After the trial run, no invitation code will be required for open user registration.
“
Journalists registered and used their accounts according to instructions on the SEC’s “Fund E Account” website, completing the process in just minutes. The entire procedure involved four steps: user registration, real-name authentication, fund account binding, and public offering fund inquiry.
After completing this step of real-name authentication, clicking on the “Asset Fund Binding” button allows journalists to see all their purchased fund products from various fund sales platforms listed in the binding options (which can be linked to an account). After successful binding, they will be able to intuitively view their total investment in funds and start using the query function.
It is worth noting that the Fund E account only provides query services to investors and does not allow redemption transactions.
The data dates displayed in the Fund E account are generally three trading days ahead of the date on which the user requested the query (T-day).
For example, if a “fund E account” is opened on February 10, the assets page shows total assets, fund shares, and net fund value corresponding to the date three trading days ahead of that date, i.e., February 7.
