Many data decline, Taiwan's economy starts the year poorly - www.chinanews.com
Shanghai-based Xinhua News Agency reported that exports reached “five black” in January, with the manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) falling for seven consecutive months and consumer prices rising to the “three digits.” Taiwan’s authorities have recently released economic data for January 2023.
Experts say that Taiwan’s economy is underperforming in the new year and growth pressures are mounting.
According to the Taiwan authorities' financial affairs department, Taiwan's exports in January this year amounted to $31.51 billion, down 21.2 per cent year-on-year, and negative growth for the fifth consecutive month.
Exports in all 11 major export categories declined compared to the same period last year.
Plastic rubber and its products and optical equipment suffered the greatest decline, with a year-on-year decline of 37.6 per cent and 35.7 per cent, respectively.
Electronic component exports fell 20.1% year-on-year, marking the largest decline in 11 years.
Of these, integrated circuits fell by 18.3 per cent annually, the largest decline in 14 years.
Chang Mei-na, director of the Statistics Department at this ministry, said that it reflects the diffusion of the weak demand effect in the consumer electronics industry and its entry into correction mode.
Statistics show that in January, both imports and exports of Taiwan region fell, and the excess amount of exports was only 2.34 billion US dollars, which is the lowest level in the past three years.
The Taiwan authorities' financial services department believes that global terminal demand is declining, industry adjusts inventories to suppress the willingness of manufacturers to purchase, and exports are unlikely to improve in the short term, and Taiwan's exports decline in the first quarter of this year is more likely than expected.
According to the Taiwan China Economic Research Institute, the seasonally adjusted Taiwan Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index (PMI) in January was 40.4%, a decrease of 3.3 percentage points from December last year, and contracted for seven consecutive months.
In the system of economic monitoring indicators, the PMI is 50% as the boom line, and an index greater than 50% represents expansion, and the opposite, contraction.
In January, the five components of the Taiwan PMI showed contracting new orders, production and employment, declining supplier delivery times and stock contracting.
The six major industries that reported PMI contraction were: electrical power and mechanical equipment (35.1%), electronics and optics (35.2%), chemicals and biotechnology and medical (39.2%), basic raw materials (42.4%), transportation (42.6%) and food and textiles (45.7%).
In terms of prices, the Taiwan authorities’ “Controller General Office” announced that the annual CPI growth rate in January this year was 3.04%, again breaking the 3% mark since July last year.
Among them, the price of vegetables soared by 28.25%, creating a new high in 17 months.
According to Cao Zhihong, a special commissioner of Taiwan’s “General Comptroller’s Office,” the increase in vegetable prices is indeed higher than expected, and if the Spring Festival factor is excluded, the average CPI in January and February should be close to the 2.71% of last December, and inflationary pressures are still present and remain high.
Looking forward to this year's Taiwan economy, experts expressed pessimism after comprehensive reports by local media such as United Daily News and Yahoo Finance.
Wu Dajin, a professor of economics at Taiwan’s Central University, analyzes that the export downturn may cause cash flow problems for export-oriented manufacturers and raise the risk of debt default.
At the same time, declining orders have forced manufacturers to cut labor costs, which in turn affects the labor market and household incomes, thereby undermining consumer spending power.
According to the Taiwan Institute of Economic Research researcher, Chu Dasheng, the inflation situation in Europe and the United States remains unresolved this year, demand continues to contract, and the Taiwan export recession is expected to continue into the first half of the year.
Taiwan’s economy is export-driven; its growth will be weaker than last year because of sluggish exports.
Did the Balloon Incident Brighten America's Eyes?
Strengthen restrictions on technology exports to China
According to a report by the Wall Street Journal today, the United States is preparing to further tighten the export of technology to China after the balloon incident.
Current and former security officials say the balloon incident underscores the national security threat posed by China and will help generate more political support for beefing up U.S. technology protections.
The United States claimed that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence collection and communication.
According to Martijn Rasser, a former senior CIA official and now at the Washington think tank New America Security Center.
"This is undoubtedly adding fuel to the fire and supports the hard-line view against China."
“We will also consider taking more extensive action to expose and respond to China’s larger-scale surveillance activities that pose a threat to our national security and to our allies and partners,” White House Press Secretary Karine Jean-Pierre told reporters on Thursday.
US officials said they had informed more than 30 governments about the balloon incident, and that international coordination was crucial to address the Chinese threat.
Emily Benso, a senior researcher at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, says that, in addition to the Biden administration’s actions, the newly formed House Committee on Strategic Competition between the US and the Chinese Communist Party may also put pressure on the US to take tougher measures to slow China’s development.
She said that lawmakers would feel increasing pressure to take a tougher stance, which could push the White House to adopt a more aggressive policy.
The Wall Street Journal said that many people advocating for stricter export controls are also pushing to expand the scope of the controls to include industries such as artificial intelligence.
The U.S. government is also developing a foreign investment review plan to examine whether U.S. investments overseas pose potential national security threats from China.
Analysts say the White House may face calls for a faster launch of the plan.
First batch of personal pension products launched for sale, with the shortest holding period of only 360 days - chinanews.com
Personal pension wealth management products were launched for the first time.
The 7 products offered by the home institution can be selected, with the shortest holding period being 360 days.
Personal retirement financial products are finally online.
On February 10, China Financial Network released the first list of personal pension financial products, seven of the personal pension financial products of the Industrial Bank of China, the Agricultural Bank of China and the Postal Bank of China were officially released.
At this point, the "shelves" of the personal pension account are finally full of four types of products: personal pension savings, personal pension investment, personal pension insurance, and publicly offered mutual funds.
It is reported that all of the first batch of individual pension products are open-ended net-value type public offerings, with 5 new issues and 2 existing ones; except for one product which is a mixed-type, the remaining six products are fixed-income types.
The Beijing Youth Daily reporters found that 4 out of the 5 new products were from ICBC Wealth Management, all of which were fixed income products, and the shortest holding period was 365 days, 540 days, 720 days, and 1080 days, respectively, and the corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90%, and 5.25% - 5.75%.
The remaining new product, “Postbank 富裕增益·鸿锦最短持有1095天第1号,” also a fixed-income product, was issued on February 10 and closed on February 19, with a risk rating of Level 2.
Of the two products that remain, one is the 360-day technology-innovative renminbi investment product “Nongxin Tongxin Flexible”, which is a mixed investment class with a risk rating of level three.
Another product that is still available is "Postal Savings Wealth Additional Yinhe Hongjin Minimum Holding Period 365 Days No. 1," a fixed income product. It started collecting funds on December 30 last year and officially started operating on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net value on February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the State Council Office's Opinion on Promoting the Development of Personal Pensions, the funds of the personal pension fund account can be invested in financial products such as bank accounts, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, public equity funds, etc.
The first personal pension wealth management product was sold, marking that personal pension investors can officially purchase wealth management products through the personal pension fund account.
The China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission formulated the Interim Measures for the Management of Personal Pension Business of Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies in November last year.
The Scheme provides that participants may purchase personal pension products such as personal retirement savings, personal retirement financial products, personal retirement insurance products, and personal retirement public fund products through the personal retirement fund account.
Subsequently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Affairs, the Ministry of Finance and the National Taxation Bureau issued circulars specifying that the personal pension system would be implemented in Beijing, Tianjin, and 36 pioneer cities and regions, including Shijiazhuang, the Yunnan New District and Jincheng City in Shandong Province.
As of December 31, 2022, there were 19.5 million participants in personal pension plans, with 6.13 million individuals contributing to them and total contributions amounting to RMB 1.42 billion.
Previously, the banks participating in the pilot had only listed three types of products: personal pension savings, personal pension insurance products and personal pension public funds.
Now that a variety of personal pension wealth management products have gathered together, how should investors choose?
Experts from the Jilin Bank Product Development Department said that compared with other personal pension products, both pilot-stage pension-linked wealth management products and individual pension-linked wealth management products have three characteristics.
First, the banks are more robust, with more robust risk management mechanisms, investment strategies and concepts, and independent third-party custodianship by non-mother banks.
II. Long-term nature, with most pilot phase pension products having maturities of five years or more; in the next issuance of individual pension products, the minimum holding period is generally one year, and encouraging a holding period of three years or more.
Third, it is inclusive. The threshold for purchasing products is low, and the starting point is generally 1 yuan, and some are as low as 0.01 yuan. The fees such as custody fees and management fees are more favorable.
Professionals noted that investors had to make their choices based on product characteristics and their own risk tolerance.
Individual pension savings have characteristics of long-term duration, high interest rates, and high safety, making them suitable for individuals with low risk tolerance; individual pension insurance products focus on protection, making them more appropriate for those who cannot bear investment risks but can accept stable returns; while individual pension product and open-end fund products do not guarantee returns or yields, they carry some investment risks, yet offer higher expected returns, which are more suitable for individuals with certain financial knowledge and higher risk tolerance.
Article/Reporter: Cheng Jie; Coordination: Chai Hua Bo
Newly Appointed Members of the Central Committee, Alternate Members, and Provincial and Ministerial Level Main Leaders Complete Study Course on Learning and Implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress Spirit - Rolling News - Huasheng Online - Hunan Daily
The seminar for new members, alternate members and provincial and ministerial leading cadres of the Central Committee on studying and implementing the thoughts of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era and the 20th CPC National Congress was concluded.
February 11, 2023 at 1:07 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large | medium | small】
Xinhua News Agency Beijing February 10th Message - The seminar for the newly elected members, alternate members and leading cadres of the provincial and ministerial level on learning and implementing the thoughts of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era and the 20th CPC National Congress was concluded in the Central Party School (National Administrative College) on the afternoon of the 10th. Cai Qi, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Secretary of the Central Commission for Discipline Inspection, attended the conclusion ceremony and made a summary speech.
He said that we should deeply study and implement the important spirit of General Secretary Xi Jinping's speech at the opening ceremony of the seminar, more firmly embrace the "two establishments", resolutely do the "two safeguards", enhance our capabilities, and work hard to push forward all aspects of Chinese-style modernization, and create a performance that can stand the test of history, practice and people in the process of building a socialist modernized country in all respects and promoting the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants were guided by Xi Jinping's ideas of socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era, carefully studied the spirit of the 20th Party Congress and the important speech of the General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar, and engaged in in-depth discussions and exchanges in connection with practical activities. They deepened their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues of Chinese-style modernization, strengthened their confidence and determination to comprehensively advance the great revival of the Chinese nation with Chinese-style modernization under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee, with Comrade Xi Jinping as its core, and strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission to fulfil their duties, do their work well and ensure a good start to the new era.
At the closing ceremony, 10 workshop delegates made presentations and shared their learnings.
Cai Qi said that learning and implementing the thoughts of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress is both the primary political task of the present and the future, and a long-term strategic task. It is necessary to promote learning and implementation in-depth, thorough and sincere, in accordance with the requirements of "comprehensive learning, comprehensive understanding, and comprehensive implementation".
We must understand more deeply the decisive significance of the "two establishments", firmly uphold the central position of Xi Jinping, uphold the central authority of the Party and centralize the unified leadership, continuously improve the political judgment, political understanding and political execution, and always maintain a high degree of consistency in ideas, politics and action with the Party Central Committee, which has comrade Xi Jinping as its core.
We should strive to master the basic skills of Marxist theory, consciously use the innovative theory of the Party to arm our minds, guide our practice and promote our work, and work hard in deep study, profound understanding and sincere practice, so as to truly learn with firm belief, learn with absolute loyalty and learn with a sense of mission and responsibility.
We must implement the decisions of the 20th National Congress of the Party with a spirit of enthusiasm and commitment, firmly advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves and get ready, and act as a good "construction team leader" to turn the blueprint into reality step by step.
We must keep in mind that the comprehensive and strict control of the Party is always on the way, and the Party's self-revolution is always on the way. We must firmly implement the political responsibility of the comprehensive and strict control of the Party, and take the political construction of the Party as our guiding principle, and make a great stride forward in the new great project of building the Party of the new era.
To strengthen the ability to drive high-quality development, serve the people, and prevent and resolve risks, we should vigorously develop the spirit of investigation and research, and resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucratism.
Xi Jinping, Li Keqiang, Li Shiwei, Chen Wenquing, Liu Jinkun, Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, and Chen Si presided over the ceremony.
East Germany's last Communist Prime Minister is dead.
The successor of the East German Communist Party reported in a party statement, “Last night, Hans Modrow left us at the age of 95.
Our party has thus lost an important leader.
“
On November 13, 1989, four days after the opening of the Berlin Wall, which separated East Berlin and West Berlin for 28 years, Modrow said he would help turn East Germany into a democratic country.
At that time, the Communist Party leaders were forced to step down as protesters across East Germany demanded democracy and freedom.
When Mikhail Gorbachev came to power in the Soviet Union, he called for change in Soviet-dominated Eastern Europe.
In March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free election in the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The election results led to him no longer serving as Prime Minister.
Despite Mordor's reforms, opponents accused him of trying to delay the political changes and reunification that took place in October 1990.
He was also criticized for trying to rebuild, rather than abolish, the secret police.
In 1993, Modrow was convicted of electoral fraud in the May 1989 municipal elections, but he was not jailed.
These allegations were allegedly politically motivated.
From 1990 to 1994, Modrow continued to serve in the German Bundestag and from 1999 to 2004, he was a Member of the European Parliament.
Mudros sees himself as a reformer and wants to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want the return of the old East Germany, but that East Germany’s achievements should be recognized.
Modrow was born in 1928 in the then German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica in Poland), and was trained as a mechanic.
During World War II, he served as the leader of a youth fire brigade and, towards the end of the conflict, became a member of the Nazi militia Volkssturm, which recruited men aged 16 to 60 to join the final struggles of the war.
At the age of 17, Modrow was captured by the Soviet army and taken as a prisoner of war to the Soviet Union, where he attended anti-Fascist courses and became a committed Communist.
In 1949, the year of the establishment of East Germany, he returned to his home country and found a job as a mechanic. He continued to study social sciences and economics and obtained a doctorate.
Modrow was a staff member of the Free German Youth movement, which almost all East German young people joined, and rose to become the chairman of the party in the Dresden region between 1973 and 1989 through the ruling Socialist Unity Party (SED).
He also served in the East German parliament for more than 30 years.
In 1990, Modrow became the de facto leader of East Germany and held the highest state office.
Hanoi, Vietnam – The official visit of Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet and his wife to Singapore and Brunei has been successful and has yielded comprehensive, practical and concrete results, according to the Vietnamese news agency VNA.
In the three days of his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng participated in more than 30 different activities.
The results achieved have given new impetus to the ongoing development of the Viet Nam-New Zealand strategic partnership and the Vietnamese-New Zealand comprehensive partnership in a deeper, broader and more effective direction.
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Triet continued to reaffirm the foreign policy of the Vietnamese Party and the State, namely, independence, autonomy, pluralism, diversity, willingness to be a good friend and reliable partner of all countries and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in each country’s interest to promote the welfare of its people and contribute to regional and global peace, stability, and development.
In various meetings and talks, Prime Minister Pham Minh Khai and the leaders of Singapore and Brunei agreed to continue to enhance political mutual trust with Viet Nam through the exchange of high-level delegations, the effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and the important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Viet Nam signed a Memorandum of Understanding on a Green and Digital Economy Partnership with Singapore.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
During meetings with business leaders, colloquia and economic forums, Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet stressed that Viet Nam welcomes and facilitates the expansion of investments by Singaporean and Bruneian companies in the fields of digital transformation, green energy, high technology, innovative ideas and other areas in Viet Nam.
The visit not only helped to deepen Viet Nam &apos; s cooperation with Singapore and Brunei in various traditional areas of politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defence, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, civil exchanges, etc., but also created a framework for cooperation between the countries in new potential areas such as digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovative ideas, smart cities, sustainable development, etc.
King Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei and Prime Minister Phan Mạnh Quỳnh are preparing to enter into bilateral talks.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
During the visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh arranged time to visit and listen to the thoughts and wishes of the Vietnamese community living in the localities.
During the meetings between the two leaders, Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet recommended that the authorities of both countries pay more attention to and create favourable conditions for the local Vietnamese community to be treated fairly, to have the opportunity to contribute to local society and to foster bilateral relations.
The proposal was agreed upon and supported by both leaders.
In particular, Prime Minister Fan Myung-jin also shared with the two leaders the aspiration for an ASEAN community of unity, peace, stability and prosperity; and agreed to remain united with ASEAN countries and to enhance the central role of ASEAN in the complex and changing context of the regional and international situation.
With the important results achieved, Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet &apos; s official visits to Singapore and Brunei contributed positively to the effective implementation of the outward route of the Thirteenth Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam, which prioritizes the strengthening of relations with ASEAN neighbours, the effective implementation of the Conclusion No. 12 of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of Vietnam on the work of Vietnamese expatriates in the new situation (12-KL/TW) and the use of the strength of all-national solidarity.
(Finish)
NEWS GOV-MO: Police announcement: Police Department calls on citizens to beware of fake telecom companies scam text messages
Recently, the Police Bureau received multiple reports of telecommunications fraud cases where criminals impersonated local telecom companies and sent fraudulent SMSs containing links to fake websites, promising rewards for exchanging points that were about to expire.
The owner entered the credit card details and the verification code as instructed and immediately received a notification from the financial institution that the credit card had an unknown consumption record and that the credit card details were suspected of having been stolen from the aforementioned website.
The investigation confirmed that the telecommunications company concerned had not sent the aforementioned text message.
The police urge the public to be vigilant when receiving similar text messages and not to click on the links in the text messages or provide any personal information. If you are asked to provide credit card information, account transaction passwords or transaction verification codes, you should be doubly cautious to prevent credit card theft.
Scam alert:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity information and improve personal prevention awareness.
Do not casually log onto unknown websites and register your personal and credit card information there to prevent identity theft;
3. Beware of fake websites and phishing websites, and always pay attention to whether the website address is completely consistent with the official website.
4. Install antivirus software on your mobile phone, mobile device or computer and update it regularly.
If you suspect that you have been a victim of fraud or any other crime, please contact the Police Commissioner's Fraud Reporting Hotline at 8800 7777 or the Crime Report Line at 993 for assistance immediately.
EU summit debates refugee policy, EU officials: reception process is a bottleneck - China News Network
EU summit is in a dilemma over the refugee policy, and EU officials said that every step of the reception process has bottlenecks
According to a report by Agence France-Presse on February 10, at the latest EU summit on that day, the President of the European Commission, von der Leyen, said that the leaders of the European Union agreed to introduce stricter policies on illegal immigrants, so that it would be easier to expel illegal immigrants.
The EU’s move is reportedly in response to growing concerns about illegal immigration in Europe, where the core problem today is that few illegal migrants are eventually repatriated.
According to the summit document, EU leaders called on the Commission to “immediately mobilize substantial EU funds” to strengthen external borders through infrastructure and surveillance.
However, the EU has been quarrelsome with its member States on issues such as the payment of the fence costs.
Von der Leyen has repeatedly stated that EU funds will not cover the costs involved.
But some member state diplomats said that if the EU could share the cost of installing cameras, watchtowers and other infrastructure along its external borders, it would free up national budgets and speed up the construction process.
According to the European Euractiv website, EU officials have admitted that bottlenecks exist at every step of the refugee reception process, that limited reception capacity and overburdened immigration authorities in member states cannot prevent refugees from filing “numerous” asylum applications across the EU, and that the EU’s reception system is in an almost “eternal crisis.”
The European Commission estimates that in 2017, EU Schengen countries received over 920,000 asylum applications, up nearly half from the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded more than 330,000 illegal entry cases last year.
In this context, the summit also agreed on a "principle" that EU countries could deport illegal immigrants back to their home countries based on a court decision of another member country.
In addition, EU leaders reportedly agreed to “increase the use of the concept of safe states,” which would pave the way for the EU to develop a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
The Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Xia Lijiang, visited China to convey the message of Song Tao: welcome the Green Party to visit China under the consensus of 92.
The Vice Chairman of the Chinese Nationalist Party in Taiwan, Shih Lien-jang, met with the Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, Song Tao, and the member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, Wang Meng.
Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor of the Nationalist Party’s official institution, the Guoguang Foundation, was interviewed by the Central News Agency of Taiwan yesterday evening. He actively praised Song Taizheng for his words to Xia Litian, saying that China welcomes Green Party people to visit the mainland as long as they acknowledge the “92 Consensus” and are against Taiwan independence.
The Nationalist Party considered it a new thing.
Xia Liyan met with Song Tao earlier that day, but the news did not mention this claim.
The ruling Democratic Progressive Party in Taiwan has been clarifying its refusal to accept the “92 Consensus.”
According to Central News Agency today, the delegation led by the Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Shali Lian, visited the mainland. During their stay in Beijing, they met with the member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee Wang Meng, the new Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, Song Tao, and the Secretary of the Beijing Municipal Committee, Yin Li.
In an interview with Song Tao, Xi Liyen said that the political basis of the Communist Party of China was the "Consensus of 92" and anti-Taiwan independence, while Zhao Chunshan, a senior adviser to the Nationalist Party's State Policy Foundation, said that the Nationalist Party's "Consensus of 92" was the true "Consensus of 92".
Zhao Chunshan notes that this is different from his previous experiences at meetings.
Recently, I had a video conference with scholars from the mainland, and in this conference, I did not hear any words about the suppression of Taiwan and the “anti-secession law”. Instead, the focus was on the resumption of exchanges and dialogue.
Zhao Chunshan pointed out that the two sides were in a dangerous situation, and the mainland of China hoped to convey its intention to improve relations through the Kuomintang.
Because there is no mutual trust between the CPC and the other party, the latter is still willing to work well for the Taiwanese, and the delegate does not want to damage relations between the two sides.
According to Zhao Chunshan, Wang Hongwen also personally gave instructions to Song Tao to tell "you must implement the requests made by them (Taiwanese farmers and fishermen)" and if it is not possible to solve it comprehensively, it should be handled on a case-by-case basis.
The report did not mention whether the Nationalist Party delegation visiting the mainland directly referred to the daily overflights of Chinese military aircraft and warships, the agricultural and fisheries problems in Taiwan's few counties and cities, or whether the Central News Agency reporters were interviewed to raise such issues.
What exactly was the “object” shot down over Alaska?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
On Friday afternoon (10 February), the United States military again used the most advanced American stealth jet fighter F-22 to shoot down an unidentified object flying over Alaska, United States.
The crash site is ten miles from the coast of Alaska.
This is the second time in less than a week that the US military has shot down an airborne object.
Last Saturday, a spy balloon from China was shot down off the coast of South Carolina, several days after drifting over US airspace.
The Pentagon said the second object shot down entered US airspace over the north-east of Alaska on Thursday night and was tracked by the US military as it moved at an altitude of 12,000 metres (40,000 feet), about the size of a small car, much smaller than the previous Chinese spy balloon.
The Pentagon still believes that there is no evidence to suggest that this object can be controlled.
The White House's National Security Council's strategic communications coordinator, John Coy, said on Friday that although the specific appearance of the flying object in the sky was unclear, it "posed a reasonable threat to the safety of civil aviation."
Kobe said that this object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which does not have an attached payload.
Kobe said, "We call it an 'object' because it's the best description we can give it at this point."
President Biden listened to the Pentagon’s advice before ordering the object to be shot down, and he was “very careful” in making that decision, Corby added.
The United States official description of the object can be summarized roughly as: the size of a small car, without joysticks, without suspension, flying at an altitude of about 10,000 metres.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Many analyses and speculations on the Internet now suggest that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It may have come from China, as did the spy balloon that invaded US airspace and the Chinese balloon that hovered over Latin America, both of which were performing a mission in different locations.
And some have linked this “object” in Alaska to UFOs.
The US News & World Report quoted former US Congressman Peter Meijer as tweeting on Friday that "I hope that the 'UFO' was a spy balloon, not a legitimate UFO."
The irony of conflating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is striking, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, he said.
Mejia tweeted this shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
The Newsweek said that it was not only Mejer who suspected the object was a UFO.
Republican Rep. Tim Burchett from Tennessee criticized the government’s cover-up last month, calling on the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) to publish a report on “unidentified flying objects.”
Xi Jinping sent a letter to encourage the members of the Chinese medical team in Africa. They should show love and care to the local people and tell the Chinese story with their deeds. - Rolling News - Hunan Daily Network - Huasheng Online
Xi Jinping sent a letter of encouragement to the Chinese medical team in Africa, urging them to use their medical skills to help the local people and to tell the Chinese story with their deeds.
2023-02-11 13:09:10 [Source: Xinhua] [Edited by: Li Shufeng] Font:【Large Small Medium 】
On February 9, Xi Jinping, the Central Secretary of the CPC, the Chairman of the State Council and the Chairman of the Central Military Committee, sent a letter to the members of the 19th Chinese medical team that assisted the Central African Republic, greeting them and the large number of foreign medical aid teams and expressing his earnest hopes.
In his reply, Xi Jinping said that you are white angels who save lives and heal wounds and friendly messengers who spread love, and you have overcome difficulties in work and life in China-Africa and served the local people with heart.
This year marks the 60th anniversary of China’s dispatching medical teams abroad; I extend sincere greetings to all comrades who have and continue to serve in international medical missions.
Xi Jinping pointed out that China’s people love peace and cherish life, which is vividly illustrated in medical aid missions abroad.
I hope that you will not forget your original intention and remember your mission, and vigorously carry forward the spirit of the Chinese medical team of not being afraid of hardship, being willing to make sacrifices, saving lives and treating injuries, and showing boundless love. Use your kindness and medical skills to benefit the local people, tell the Chinese story with practical actions, and make greater contributions to promoting the construction of a community with a shared future for mankind.
Foreign medical assistance is an important component of China's foreign aid work.
In 1963, China sent its first medical team abroad to Algeria.
Over six decades, China has dispatched over 300,000 medical personnel to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, America, Europe, and Oceania, treating more than 290 million patients, winning widespread acclaim from the international community.
Currently, the team operates in 115 health centres in 56 countries worldwide, almost half of which are in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th batch of China’s medical teams dispatched to Central Africa wrote letters to President Xi Jinping, reporting on their efforts in implementing the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and providing medical services for local residents, as well as expressing their determination to contribute to building a community with a shared future for mankind.
Iran celebrates anniversary of revolution Hackers who support protests shock president's TV speech
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official rally on Saturday to mark the 44th anniversary of the Iranian revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ibrahim Raisi’s television address.
The president's live television address was interrupted on the Internet for about a minute, with a logo of a group of anti-Iranian government hackers named "Edalat Ali" appearing on the screen.
A voice also appeared shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic".
Reuters reports that Iran is commemorating its revolution anniversary and hackers have disrupted national TV broadcasts.
As Iran officially commemorates the 44th anniversary of the Iranian revolution, Raisi’s hardline government faces the boldest challenge from young protesters who are calling for its ouster, but Raisi still calls on “deceived youth” to repent so that they can be pardoned by Iran’s supreme leader.
National protests continue in Iran after the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini in September while in custody of the country’s moral police.
The Iranian security forces’ deadly crackdown on protests is one of the strongest challenges the Islamic Republic has faced since the 1979 revolution overthrew the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of a general amnesty to mark the anniversary of the 1979 revolution, Iranian authorities on Friday released jailed dissident Farhad Meysami and Iranian-French scholar Fariba Adelkhah, who had been on hunger strike.
Earlier, the Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty decree, which includes some prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to human rights organization HRANA, as of Friday, 528 protesters had been killed, including 71 minors.
It is reported that 70 more government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and the official media have been calling for voting at Saturday &apos; s rallies to show opposition to the protests and support for the Government.
On Friday night, the night of the Iranian Revolution’s anniversary, the official media showed fireworks as part of the government-sponsored celebrations, with people shouting “Allahu Akbar!”
(God is greatest!)".
However, many people were heard shouting "Down with the dictator!"
and the 'death of the Islamic Republic' in videos posted on social media.
Saturday, the government TV broadcast live footage of official gatherings across all states.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestically produced anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lesley’s speeches were frequently interrupted by the slogan “America Die” – a symbol of the state’s rallying.
The crowd also shouted "Death to Israel".
Reuters said that Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, which is a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 for national security offences.
They later placed her under house arrest, but she returned to prison in January.
Adelkhah denied these allegations.
A week before Mesaimi was released, his supporters warned that he was at risk of death due to his hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting against the compulsory wearing of headscarves.
The French Foreign Ministry called for Adelkhah’s release on Friday, calling for her freedom to be restored, “including her being allowed to return to France if she so wishes.”
“
The Sixteenth China-Japan Energy and Environmental Comprehensive Forum was held in Beijing; He Li Feng attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua News Agency reported that the Sixteenth Forum on Comprehensive Environmental and Energy Conservation between China and Japan was held in Beijing via online and offline channels on February 11th.
Hu Lifeng, member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and director of the National Development and Reform Commission, attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
Huang Lifeng noted that hosting this forum is an important step in implementing the consensus reached at the joint meeting between President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Fumio Kishida in Bangkok to strengthen green development cooperation between China and Japan.
China will fully implement the spirit of the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China, accelerate the green transformation of development methods, make great strides in combating environmental pollution, comprehensively strengthen resource conservation, actively and steadily promote carbon neutrality to the highest level, and promote carbon reduction, pollution reduction, greening and growth in synergy, as well as ecological priority, energy-efficiency and green low-carbon development.
China is willing to work with Japan to deepen cooperation in green and low-carbon industries, technology, policy dialogue, and people-to-people exchanges, driving further progress in bilateral green development cooperation.
Japanese Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry Hiroshige Sekimoto attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
The forum is jointly organized by the National Development and Reform Commission of China, the Ministry of Commerce of China, the Ministry of Economy and Trade of Japan, and the Japanese-Chinese Economic Association, featuring a main forum and four sub-forums on energy efficiency improvement, automotive electrification and automation, hydrogen energy, and long-term trade between China and Japan.
Representatives of Chinese and Japanese governments, enterprises and institutions exchanged views.
Q&A: How to view the U.S. January non-farm employment data greatly exceeded expectations and future trends - Economic Observation Network - Professional financial news website
Q: How do you view the unexpectedly strong January non-farm employment data from the US and its future trends?
A: On February 3, the US Department of Labor announced the non-farm employment data in January 2023, with 51.7 thousand new non-farm employment, which is significantly higher than the market expectation of 18.9 thousand; the unemployment rate fell to 3.4%, the lowest in nearly 50 years; the hourly wage growth rate was 4.4% year-on-year and 0.3% month-on-month, with slight slowdown.
In terms of the total amount, there are many one-time and technical factors that affect the data, such as the return to work of teachers on strike, the revision of the survey and statistical scope, and the update of the seasonal factor. It is expected that there will be some adjustments in the future (refer to the new non-farm payrolls added in January 2022, which were revised from 50.4 thousand to 36.4 thousand); non-farm employment is not as strong as the data shows.
Structurally, the impact of layoffs in high-tech enterprises remains, but is relatively low; new employment in high-contact services such as leisure hotels, education and health care has recovered significantly, and data show that the labour force gap in services remains.
Combined with a similarly over-expected recovery in the services PMI, job vacancy and labor gap data, and strong consumer credit data, we judge that the US services sector is recovering rapidly after extreme weather and holidays.
We believe that supply-demand tensions in the US job market will hardly improve without a recession.
Currently, there is still a supply gap of over 5 million in US labor markets, with labor participation rates rising slowly, especially among those aged 25 to 54 who have already reached their pre-pandemic peak.
In addition, strong consumer demand, due to excess savings and consumer credit among American residents, will further delay the impact of austerity on the job market.
The US economy will be underpinned by continued supply-demand tensions in the US job market in 2023.
In addition, with the interest rate hikes now nearing their end and inflation expectations repeating themselves, we are not optimistic about the continued slowdown in wage growth.
Before this data was released, US equity-bond markets were overly optimistic about the Fed’s rate-hiking path.
As inflation data continued to improve, the Fed maintained a balance between shortening the pace of interest rate hikes and preserving the fragile balance of market inflation expectations. However, the market ignored the Fed's hawkish statements and expected not only an early end to interest rate hikes but also two rate cuts by the end of the year.
With labor market supply and demand tight and the impact of austerity uncertain, we believe the Fed’s guidance for rate hikes at the end of the year is relatively reasonable, and the market’s extremely anticipated adjustment and trading crowds may cause some harm.
However, the persistence of wage growth will not reverse the current rapidly declining trend in inflation. As M2 data turns negative year-on-year and the leading indicators of the various CPI sub-elements gradually improve, the US CPI data has moved into a rapidly declining phase since October, the persistence of wage growth will only form a base for future inflation data, and the current market expectations are difficult to falsify, and the market will enter a new round of play after the next inflation data is released.
Shenzhen: to build the first and leading ultra-speed pioneer city in China and the world - chinanews.com
Xinhua News Agency reported on February 11th that the Shenzhen Industrial and Information Technology Bureau has recently issued the “Action Plan for Building an Ultra-fast Pioneer City of Shenzhen”.
It is proposed that by the end of 2023, a super broadband network with high rates, large capacity, and low latency will be built to achieve the goal of “Dual Gigabit, Full Optical Network, 1 millisecond, Everything Connected,” making it China’s first and world-leading city in terms of ultra-fast speed.
The plan proposes to speed up the upgrade of the gigabit optical network.
By the end of 2023, the share of 10G PON ports will reach 100%, and the number of all-optical industrial parks (industrial parks) will exceed 100.
The plan calls for an overall improvement in 5G network efficiency.
Research and formulate Shenzhen 5G network service quality standards, carry out 5G network testing and evaluation, and improve the quality of 5G network services.
Support basic telecommunications enterprises to increase the optimization of 5G networks in key regions and places, and add 10,000 new 5G base stations throughout the year. The average download speed in the city reached 500Mbps and the upload speed reached 100Mbps. The download speed in key regions reached 1000Mbps and the upload speed reached 200Mbps. The network speed and user experience have been greatly improved.
Build a high-quality wireless local area network at the city level.
Developing wireless local area network (WLAN) service specifications for public places, promoting the upgrade of WLANs in areas with high population density and concentrated information consumption needs throughout the city, and providing gigabyte access capacity.
Based on "Shen I Net", build a unified authentication and management platform for public wireless local area networks in the whole city, realize "one-time authentication, seamless roaming, and smart switching", and support operating entities to include social self-built APs with public service capabilities in the authentication and management platform.
By the end of 2023, the total number of upgraded access points will be no less than 20,000.
In addition, the Plan proposes to build high-quality all-optical carrier networks, build multi-tier computing power supply systems, accelerate the construction of key communications network facilities and improve the capacity of Internet application services.
The Plan clearly states that a cooperative construction of the Internet of Things sensing system should be carried out.
Explore building management models for urban perception terminal construction based on the “open-source HarmonyOS” operating system to lower integration costs and accelerate the development of city-level IoT perception platforms. Promote interconnectivity and data interoperability among various municipal IoT platform networks and professional IoT platform networks.
Deepen the application of IoT sensing in the fields of urban management, public services, public safety, transportation and travel, and expand the collection of fixed sensing data in urban roads, buildings, public facilities and mobile sensing data in smart connected cars.
By the end of 2023, the number of hydroelectric IoT sensor terminals will exceed 9 million, and 20 multifunctional smart pole application demonstration projects will be built.
The plan also noted that efforts will be made to strengthen satellite-ground communication integration applications, lay out low-altitude network infrastructure construction, and promote deep coverage of 5G networks at sea.
At the same time, we will advance 5G network deep coverage at sea, build an innovation ecosystem for industry development, and support hosting top-level events and activities.
(CNBC)
How can Chinese e-commerce industry bring in “new variables” and make “content is king” a reality?
- China News Network
China News Network, February 11, 2012. Subject: China’s e-commerce industry is emerging as a “new variable,” and how can content be king?
Xia Bin, a reporter from China Finance News
“We came into e-commerce late, but we realized from the start that content was important if you wanted to stand out from the millions of stores.
Fangfang, an 90s girl from Guangdong who runs a health food store on Douyin e-commerce, has made her offline business that has been around for over three decades blossom online.
Imitating the old Hong Kong film look and adding classic Cantonese songs, click on @Fangfang's One-Dish Wok account to see stunning videos that will leave you breathless.
At the recent Douyin E-commerce “Find Your Peers · Showcase of High-Quality Content Sharing” event, Fangfang, as an example of a high-quality creator, gave a speech on her daily creative experiences and insights.
She said: "The video was well-crafted and attracted a lot of attention from netizens, many of whom were interested in my homemade ingredients and wanted to help me make delicious food, and the sales channel opened immediately.
“
Fang Fang’s video of making soups has helped more people fall in love with “Guangdong flavors,” and one livestream sold as many as 300, 000 pieces of tonics for her family-run store that was on the verge of closing down.
"Without content, no e-commerce," as video and live-streaming-based e-commerce continues to develop, people's expectations for and standards of online shopping have entered a new phase.
In the early days of livestreaming, the only selling point seemed to be the price advantage, with livestreamers often offering low-priced discounts to attract customers.
In recent years, phenomenal Vs like Liu Huhong and East Select, as well as many unfamiliar experts and businesses that have emerged in the vertical segmentation field, have been continuously creating high-quality content that fits their brand tone to improve long-term business results.
Gao Yaxuan from Douyin E-commerce Content Creator Operations said that in the past year, 6.27 million creators have monetized their content through Douyin E-commerce, with their creation volume increasing by over 250% and total transaction value rising more than twice.
“Behind these numbers, we can feel a thriving, vibrant author ecosystem.
Zhao Yaxian said,
The Communication Innovation and Future Media Experimental Platform of Beijing Normal University previously released the E-commerce Industry Content Ecology Health Index (ECHI) Report, which analyzed the importance of high-quality content in the current e-commerce industry from the perspective of data, and evaluated the content ecology of 27 mainstream e-commerce platforms in China using the index.
According to the above-mentioned report on the health index of the e-commerce industry content ecology, the top five are TikTok, Kuaishou, Taobao, Pinduoduo, and JD.
The report concludes that the content ecosystem of the e-commerce industry is a comprehensive concept that integrates e-commerce with content, but not all content can be integrated with e-commerce, and that good PGC (professional produced content) and UGC (user-generated content) are the quality carriers for integration with e-commerce, and that the higher the value of the content platform, the richer the scenarios for consumption and promotion, the greater the possibility of e-commerce implantation, the stronger the commercial value, and the higher the proportion of e-commerce content production and content consumption that is distributed in this gradually integrated public and private domain.
At the event, Professor Hu Guoming, of the Beijing Teachers University School of Journalism and Communication, and Chairman of the China Media Economics and Management Professional Committee, gave an analytical explanation of the report.
He said that in terms of content value, the e-commerce industry has now transitioned from "consumer accessibility" to "consumer quality", and high-quality, professional, and differentiated content is the "hard currency" of the e-commerce industry.
At the same time, content has become the fundamental and handle for the new stage of e-commerce development. Knowledge payment, professional knowledge, KOL (Key Opinion Leaders) and other PGC content have begun to become standard in e-commerce live broadcasting.
Looking forward to the future development of the e-commerce industry, Yu Kunming put forward two suggestions.
One is to promote the health and overall quality of the e-commerce content ecology from the perspective of improving the content structure, and to build positive content creation and management standards to achieve a healthy system index and dynamic balance of the e-commerce industry content ecology.
Another is to look at it from an external ecosystem perspective and achieve healthy development of content e-commerce and value collaboration and creation with the external environment.
"More data and support from artificial intelligence will be needed in the future e-commerce industry to predict stability for its development; moreover, it is essential to provide more standardized and healthy growth spaces for merchants so that enterprises, users, products, and services can achieve value synergy within an eco-system of healthy content."
(continued)
(VOA Chinese) – On Friday (February 10), the Biden administration blacklisted six Chinese entities suspected of involvement in the spy balloon program.
The US Department of Commerce stated that the five Chinese companies and one research institute were helping to modernize the Chinese military, particularly in aerospace projects, including airships and aircraft.
Blacklisted companies have difficulty accessing US technology exports.
The list is called an “entity list,” and companies that enter it will be unable to purchase technology or goods from US suppliers unless they obtain a special export license from the US Department of Commerce.
The companies listed on the blacklist are: Beijing Nanjiang Sky Space Technology Co., Ltd., China Electronics Science and Technology Group Fourth Eighth Research Institute, Dongguan Lingkong Remote Sensing Technology Co., Ltd., Eagle Gate Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd., Guangzhou Tianhai Xiang Aeronautical Technology Co., Ltd., and Shanxi Eagle Gate Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd.
Before that, the White House said it was considering more extensive measures to "expose and address" China's larger-scale surveillance activities that threaten U.S. national security.
The balloon incident has sparked further tensions between China and the US, with US Secretary of State Hillary Clinton cancelling a visit to China.
On February 4, the US shot down an air balloon, and China raised a serious protest to the US embassy in Beijing over America’s severe interference and damage to both sides’ efforts and progress toward stabilizing Sino-US relations.
Based on existing debris evidence and information from China’s military procurement platform, the US government concluded that the manufacturer of the balloon “is directly related to the People's Liberation Army,” and was approved as a supplier by the Chinese military.
At a press conference on Friday, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Mao Ning said that China has repeatedly explained the situation and clarified its position on the accidental entry of a Chinese aircraft without a pilot into United States airspace due to force majeure.
According to the State Department website, she added that the United States Congress resolution in question was purely political manipulation and hype.
China is strongly dissatisfied with this and firmly opposes it.
Matthew Axelrod, the US Department of Commerce’s Assistant Secretary for Export Enforcement, said: “Today’s action demonstrates our joint efforts to identify and stop China from using spy balloons that violate the airspace of the United States and more than 40 countries.
“
Reuters reports that an employee of Tianhai Xiang Aviation Technology Co., Ltd. in Guangzhou said he was unaware of sanctions and declined to comment further.
The Chinese Embassy in the United States has not yet commented on this information.
(Reuters et al.)
