The products are okay, but the after-sales service of Amazon is really much worse than other websites.
After placing the order, I discovered that the order was wrong, but I could not cancel it, and the web page contacting online customer service was always showing the wrong link, and I could not contact it.
After delivery, the delivery person called me and said I didn't want it anymore; I wanted to cancel the order but it wasn't successful. The delivery person took it back and said they would sign for it first so that I could apply for a return.
When applying for a return, I was informed that food items cannot be returned once signed for, and I couldn't call Amazon customer service, and they said the same thing, that food items cannot be returned once signed for.
I have bought products that cannot be returned according to the policy in JD and Sunning, including milk and diapers, and I have contacted customer service to return them, and JD's diapers smell too much when opened, but I still contacted customer service to return them, but it doesn't work with Amazon.
Rules are dead, people are alive. What do you do with your customer service?
Tell me either I pick it up myself or let the delivery person buy it for me. It's not easy for the delivery person already. Why should I let the delivery person buy the thing I didn't buy myself?
Okay, I'm not withdrawing either. I collected it myself, but I have to give you a point for your service.
The earphone has a distortion and there is a background noise
This headphone is really trash, I don't know if it's my ears that are the problem or if this headphone really isn't as good as it used to be.
I bought a blue one two years ago at a local store, sound quality was good, no noise, bass was good, after two years of use it broke, I'm going to buy another one (urbeats), after all, it feels good.
I also looked at the purple one and it looks nice, but when I opened it today, I felt it was not right; it was both loud and soft.
I thought it was just the sound effects of that song and didn't give much thought to it at first, but after listening for hours I realized this problem was quite serious. Not only were there off-key notes, but also poor bass quality compared to what I had heard before. There were some additional noises, is it possible that only my purple headphones have this issue? Or could it be that the headphone manufacturing process has indeed fallen short?
It was a very disappointing evaluation.
I definitely have to return the goods tomorrow.
